│ patch_name               │ identity_calibration                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the heavily overparameterized block with a fixed CZ gate. Because CZ is           │
│                          │ self-inverse and the block is repeated six times, the total candidate unitary is exactly  │
│                          │ the identity: CZ^6 = I. The classifier therefore uses the dataset-selected Z-Z            │
│                          │ correlators directly, while retaining only the two readout calibration parameters. This   │
│                          │ reduces the parameter count from 146 to 2 and the gate count from 186 to 6, avoids        │
│                          │ unnecessary circuit optimization, and should preserve fast convergence when the selected  │
│                          │ correlators already expose the target property.                                           │
