│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ identity_calibration_only                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the highly overparameterized 24-parameter block with a parameter-free block that  │
│                          │ is exactly identity across the fixed six repetitions. Since CZ is self-inverse, applying  │
│                          │ the same CZ six times gives CZ^6 = I. The prepared state therefore reaches the            │
│                          │ dataset-designed Z-Z readout unchanged, while the trainable gain and bias retain the      │
│                          │ ability to calibrate its scale and decision threshold. This reduces total trainable       │
│                          │ parameters from 146 to 2 and gate count from 186 to 6, strongly improving parameter       │
│                          │ efficiency and convergence speed while avoiding overfitting. It is especially appropriate │
│                          │ because the current model already reaches perfect accuracy and the fixed readout          │
│                          │ correlators are supplied by the dataset.                                                  │
