│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ globally_shared_rotations                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Tie each rotation layer across all eight qubits while retaining the proven CZ chain. This │
│                          │ preserves a six-layer noncommuting RY-RZ-entangling circuit but reduces the ansatz from   │
│                          │ 24 to 2 parameters per block, lowering the total from 146 to 14 trainable parameters. The │
│                          │ repeated blocks still receive independent copies, so the circuit remains expressive       │
│                          │ enough to learn different global basis changes at each depth. Global sharing also         │
│                          │ regularizes the model toward permutation-consistent state features, should preserve fast  │
│                          │ convergence, and substantially improves parameter efficiency without adding gates or      │
│                          │ depth.                                                                                    │
